# Billing — the manager's billing page reads (M26-S14, UC-117)
# TenantContext populated from X-Tenant-ID / X-Actor-* headers (set by the BFF). MANAGER only: STAFF
# and CUSTOMER get 403. The routes carry @NoFeatureGate() and @SuspensionAccess(MANAGER_BILLING), so
# the manager of a SUSPENDED tenant still reaches them (it is the only page they can). The summary is
# never cached: it reads the committed subscription row. A tenant with no subscription row answers
# 200 { "provisioning": true } (UC-117 A9). No response ever carries a payment URL.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. pnpm infra:up
#   2. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run migration:run
#   3. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run seed
#   4. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run dev
#
# REST Client environment: select "local" in VS Code status bar

@baseUrl = {{backendUrl}}

### Summary: status, dates, items with prices, total, open charge, price changes
GET {{baseUrl}}/billing/summary
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

### Charge history, newest due date first (Pattern A): limit 1-100 (default 25), offset >= 0
GET {{baseUrl}}/billing/charges?limit=10&offset=0
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

### Out-of-range page: 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/billing/charges?limit=101
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

### Staff: 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/billing/summary
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{staffId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: STAFF

### Customer: 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/billing/charges
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER

# ── Plan reads (M26-S17, UC-136) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Plano tab: the catalog and a preview. Both are read-only: nothing is saved and the BOOKING
# removal guard is not run (it is checked at save only). MANAGER only. A read-only plan (PAST_DUE,
# operator suspension, scheduled cancel, exempt) is reported in `readOnly`, not refused here.
# A tenant with no subscription row: GET answers 200 { "provisioning": true }, the preview 404.

### Plan: catalog with tier prices, current plan, what is scheduled, readOnly, total
GET {{baseUrl}}/billing/plan
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

### Preview: add the lead form, drop booking (each change carries its effective date)
POST {{baseUrl}}/billing/plan/preview
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

{ "items": [{ "featureKey": "HOTSITE", "tier": "STANDARD" }, { "featureKey": "LEAD_FORM", "tier": "STANDARD" }] }

### Preview: chatbot tier change
POST {{baseUrl}}/billing/plan/preview
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

{ "items": [{ "featureKey": "HOTSITE", "tier": "STANDARD" }, { "featureKey": "CHATBOT", "tier": "PLUS" }] }

### Dependency unmet (loyalty without booking): 422 BILLING_FEATURE_DEPENDENCY_UNMET
POST {{baseUrl}}/billing/plan/preview
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

{ "items": [{ "featureKey": "HOTSITE", "tier": "STANDARD" }, { "featureKey": "LOYALTY", "tier": "STANDARD" }] }

### Same body for a tenant that has booking and loyalty now (booking removed, loyalty stays): 422 BILLING_FEATURE_HAS_DEPENDENTS
POST {{baseUrl}}/billing/plan/preview
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

{ "items": [{ "featureKey": "HOTSITE", "tier": "STANDARD" }, { "featureKey": "LOYALTY", "tier": "STANDARD" }] }

### Empty selection: 422 BILLING_PLAN_EMPTY
POST {{baseUrl}}/billing/plan/preview
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

{ "items": [] }

### A feature selected twice: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/billing/plan/preview
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

{ "items": [{ "featureKey": "HOTSITE", "tier": "STANDARD" }, { "featureKey": "HOTSITE", "tier": "STANDARD" }] }

### A tier not sold for the feature: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/billing/plan/preview
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

{ "items": [{ "featureKey": "HOTSITE", "tier": "PLUS" }] }

### Staff: 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/billing/plan
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{staffId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: STAFF

### Customer: 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/billing/plan/preview
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER

{ "items": [{ "featureKey": "HOTSITE", "tier": "STANDARD" }] }

# ── Paying a charge (M26-S15, UC-119) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `chargeId` is one of the tenant's own charges: read it from GET /billing/summary (`openCharge.id`)
# or GET /billing/charges. Another tenant's id answers 404 BILLING_CHARGE_NOT_FOUND. Both routes are
# manager-only and reachable while the tenant is SUSPENDED. Locally the provider is the fake.
@chargeId = 00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000

### Payment link: 200 { status, paymentUrl, expiresAt }; a link still valid is returned as it is, an
### expired one is regenerated. A paid charge answers { status: "PAID", paymentUrl: null, expiresAt: null }.
### Errors: 409 BILLING_CHARGE_NOT_PAYABLE (cancelled, refunded, charged back), 422
### BILLING_ADDRESS_REQUIRED (a recovery charge held for the billing identity), 503
### BILLING_PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE (retryable), 404 BILLING_CHARGE_NOT_FOUND
POST {{baseUrl}}/billing/charges/{{chargeId}}/payment-link
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

### Payment return: records `payment_return_seen_at` once and refreshes the charge from the provider.
### 200 { status, paymentConfirmationPending }; never fails because the provider is unreachable.
POST {{baseUrl}}/billing/charges/{{chargeId}}/payment-return
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

### Not a UUID: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/billing/charges/not-a-uuid/payment-link
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

### Staff: 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/billing/charges/{{chargeId}}/payment-link
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{staffId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: STAFF


# ── Billing identity (M26-S16, UC-118) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The "Dados de cobrança" tab. Manager-only (STAFF / CUSTOMER 403), reachable while the tenant is
# SUSPENDED. Every PUT field is optional: a field left out is untouched; null or "" clears taxId,
# legalName and billingEmail (a BR tax id is replaced, never cleared: 422); `address` merges its sent
# sub-fields over the stored one and is validated whole (never cleared). The save takes the account
# row lock (B-I1) and never calls the provider: the identity is synced to the provider customer at
# the next charge, and a subscription held for a missing identity is issued by the next job run.
# A tenant with no billing account yet: GET answers 200 { "provisioning": true }, PUT answers
# 503 BILLING_PROVISIONING (retryable).

### Identity: 200 { provisioning: false, taxIdType, taxId (normalised), legalName, billingEmail, address }
GET {{baseUrl}}/billing/identity
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

### Save a complete BR identity: 200 with the same shape as the GET
PUT {{baseUrl}}/billing/identity
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "taxId": "529.982.247-25",
  "legalName": "Lavacar BH Ltda",
  "billingEmail": "cobranca@lavacar.com.br",
  "address": { "street": "Rua das Flores", "number": "100", "neighborhood": "Centro", "city": "Belo Horizonte", "state": "MG", "zipCode": "30130-110" }
}

### Partial update: only the sent fields change; the address merges (here only the city and ZIP)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/billing/identity
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{ "address": { "city": "Contagem", "zipCode": "32010-000" } }

### Alphanumeric CNPJ with valid check digits, punctuation and letters accepted: 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/billing/identity
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{ "taxIdType": "CNPJ", "taxId": "12.ABC.345/01DE-35" }

### Bad check digits: 422 BILLING_IDENTITY_TAX_ID_INVALID
PUT {{baseUrl}}/billing/identity
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{ "taxId": "11222333000182" }

### An empty tax id on a BR account that has one: 422 BILLING_IDENTITY_TAX_ID_INVALID, stored value kept
PUT {{baseUrl}}/billing/identity
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{ "taxId": "" }

### Invalid email: 422 BILLING_IDENTITY_EMAIL_INVALID
PUT {{baseUrl}}/billing/identity
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{ "billingEmail": "not-an-email" }

### Wrong postal code (a BR CEP is 00000-000): 400 ADDRESS_POSTAL_CODE_INVALID
PUT {{baseUrl}}/billing/identity
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{ "address": { "zipCode": "30140-07" } }

### An address still incomplete after the merge: 400 ADDRESS_FIELD_REQUIRED, nothing is saved.
### Run it against a tenant with NO stored address (a second tenant id in `tenantId`): once the
### complete save above has run, this city-only patch merges into that address and succeeds.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/billing/identity
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{ "legalName": "Half", "address": { "city": "Belo Horizonte" } }

### A body the schema refuses (a taxIdType without a taxId, a null address): 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/billing/identity
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER
Content-Type: application/json

{ "taxIdType": "CPF" }

### Staff: 403 on read and save
GET {{baseUrl}}/billing/identity
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{staffId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: STAFF

### Customer: 403
PUT {{baseUrl}}/billing/identity
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{staffId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{ "legalName": "x" }
